invariant: INV-14
file: srv_message.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: srv_certificate_fits admits one byte more than the Certificate
  message's 3-byte length field holds, so a server takes a chain whose
  message length it would write cut to its low 24 bits, a message no
  client can parse. test/srv_identity_tests.h requires one certificate
  of 2^24 - 9 bytes, and two whose lengths sum one byte past the same
  bound, to be refused.

--- old
        if (cert->der == NULL || cert->len == 0 || room < SRV_CERT_ENTRY_FRAME ||
            cert->len > room - SRV_CERT_ENTRY_FRAME) {
--- new
        if (cert->der == NULL || cert->len == 0 || room < SRV_CERT_ENTRY_FRAME ||
            cert->len > room - SRV_CERT_ENTRY_FRAME + 1) {
